otherwise. Released by closing the descriptor (record\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:399:  } while (r != 0 && errno == EINTR);\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:401:  int err = errno;\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:407: * cap is too small, or -errno. The C library's result is copied out and\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:417:  err = real ? 0 : errno;\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:427:/* rename(from, to): 0 or -errno. No copy-and-delete fallback (EXDEV fails). */\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:439:  err = r == 0 ? 0 : errno;\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:447: * O_CLOEXEC), fsync, close. 0, or the -errno of the first step that failed\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:453:  int err = fsync((int)fd) == 0 ? 0 : errno;\nnative/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:454:  int cerr = close((int)fd) == 0 ? 0 : errno;\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:7: * linked in statically; SHA-256, SHA-1 and Ed25519 are the system libcrypto's\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:18: * :jolt arm, owner ruling 1792655000000; libcrypto RAND_bytes from the same\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:25: * all 20 libcrypto entries (including RAND_bytes and EVP_sha1) this file\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:26: * resolved and the SHA-256 of that library file, so\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:36: * libcrypto's CSPRNG (RAND_bytes). A failed draw is an error status, never\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:86:  /* The same libcrypto every EVP entry resolved to: RAND_bytes draws from its\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:89:  if (RAND_bytes(out, (int)n) != 1) {\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:115:/* SHA-1 for the RFC 6455 opening handshake only (Sec-WebSocket-Accept,\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:177:/* The SHA-256 of the file at path, as 64 lowercase hex digits plus NUL. */\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:200: *  <SHA-256 hex of that file>\" into buf (not NUL-terminated); answers the\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c:206:  /* All 20 libcrypto entries, including entropy and SHA-1, must share one\nnative/jolt-crypto/jolt