rget port swaps THIS table, never the\n;; emitter: each key is a MEANING, and all seven emission sites derive their\n;; spelling from :unsafe-prefix + the safe op name (one mechanism, no per-site\n;; strings). A target without unsafe variants maps :unsafe-prefix to \"\" — every\n;; derived spelling degrades to the checked op, safe-and-slower, never wrong.\n(defn set-target! [t] (reset! (:target (cur)) t))\n(defn- target [] @(:target (cur)))\n(def ^:private target-prims\n  {:chez {:unsafe-prefix \"#3%\"}})\n(defn- unsafe-prefix [] (get-in target-prims [(target) :unsafe-prefix]))\n\n;; contagion clone sites (jolt devirt-gated fl* contagion for :num fields): a set of\n;; \"tag|proto|method\" keys for impls whose body has a :num field beside a proven\n### 6.4 Pins and the upgrade gate (owner Q5)\n\nOwner: \"record the mob's answer\", then \"opus when needed\". Jolt is pinned by\nfull SHA in `jolt-toolchain.edn`; a suitable release-tagged SHA is preferred;\nmain remains the upstream development source; nothing updates silently. The\nowner or orchestrator triggers the proposed `bb qualify:jolt-upgrade` when an\nupstream fix we need lands, when the resolved Chez version changes, or when the\npin is older than about 30 days. Age triggers evaluation, not promotion; a\nfailing candidate leaves the last passing pin.\n\nThe gate runs on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64: clean tracked load and resolved\npaths; relevant fast/all/slow tests with counts; J1 integer/CBOR/hash fixtures;\nshared VM boundary traces; J0b UDP and J0c parser/GC/cache/lifetime regressions;\nnative-library provenance; J6/J7 peers once they exist. It records candidate,\nbase and submodule SHAs, exact Chez, patches, native versions, commands, results\nand rollback coordinates. No unavailable test passes silently. Early pins\nqualify only for the implemented milestone; J8 promotion needs every parity\ngate. No numeric JVM-ratio budget exists before J8 evidence.\n\nHistorical pin and tag (W7; §13.4 ruling 4, 2026-10-20). V (read-only git\nin the local checkout, 2026-10-20): `96d7b866` is the checkout's `main`/`origin/main` head,\ncommitted 2026-10-19, carries **no tag**, and `git describe --tags` answers\n`vnightly-16-g96d7b866`; the nearest release tag the checkout knows is\n`v0.8.23` (`a0ac71c3`, 2026-10-17), with `vnightly` (`5ae108e5`, 2026-10-18) a\nmoving nightly tag. The checkout's tag list is only what it has fetched. All S\nand J0b evidence describes `96d7b866`. **J0a keeps `96d7b866`** and records it\nin `jolt-toolchain.edn` with \"tag: none; nearest release tag v0.8.23\n(a0ac71c3); describe vnightly-16-g96d7b866\". No S claim is re-established.\nFrom the first run of `qualify:jolt-upgrade` onward, Q5 governs as the owner\nstated it: a **suitable** release-tagged SHA is preferred, and an untagged SHA\nis admissible when it carries a needed upstream fix and is explicitly qualified\nthrough the gate (astra A5). No rule here mandates the newest release. A re-pin\nbefore that first gate run happens only under the reversal condition in §13.4.\n\nPin and tag (owner decision, 2026-10-22; landed `63301597`). The current\ntoolchain pins the owner fork `https://github.com/sonwh98/jolt` at\n`697b91eefabf3e964acea787cbc9cb1b6b85a28c`\n(2026-10-22T15:11:38+07:00; tag none; describe `vnightly-16-g697b91ee`;\nnearest release `v0.8.23`, `a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5`).\nFork PR `sonwh98/jolt#2` carries the Sorted fix `7b7100c1` and regenerated\nseeds `697b91ee` on upstream `75c8b610`; origin/main head `d69e5eaa`\n(PR #2 merge, tree identical to `697b91ee`); `vnightly` is now `cd4b7743`.\nThe former `0001-sorted-user-types` patch against `96d7b866` is retired;\n`:patches []` applies nothing and re-mints nothing. The patch mechanism\n(`patches/jolt/<sha>/`, `apply-patches!` in `src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`,\n`:patches` in `jolt-toolchain.edn`) remains for future patches. Seven\nsubmodule SHAs are unchanged. Seed re-mint with Chez 10.4.1 is deterministic\nacross macOS and Linux (Linux digest record `e7a39cb9`; fork seed commit\n`697b91ee`). Historical S and J0b evidence still describes `96d7b866` and is\nnot re-established by this pin move.\n\nRe-pin 2026-10-24 (owner: \"the JVM should be canonical. the other divergent\nhosts should be patched\"; jolt-lang is patched through the fork, the same\nexplicit exception as 2026-10-22). The toolchain now pins\n`b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3` (2026-10-24T13:55:46+07:00; tag\nnone; describe `vnightly-17-gb389f1a7`), fork branch `assoc-deftype-refusal`,\none commit on `697b91ee`: `assoc` on a deftype that is not Associative throws\n`ClassCastException` naming the class, as on the JVM, where it had answered a\nfresh instance (`host/chez/records-coll.ss`, the record arm of `jolt-assoc1`\nnow requires `jrec-record?`). The seed re-mint reaches its byte-fixpoint with\nno seed change; submodule SHAs are unchanged; `:patches []` still applies\nnothing. The upstream report text is in\n`collab/1792824446211-engineer-canonical-adjudication-fixes.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md`\n(the owner submits it).\n\nThis re-pin precedes the first `qualify:jolt-upgrade` run under an explicit\nowner ruling (§13.5). It was requalified by the manual gate in\n`collab/1792692000000-architect-jolt-pin-fork-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`\nsection 6: local macOS bootstrap and negative gates passed; Linux\n(defn- apply-patches!\n  [{:keys [sha dir patches]} scheme]\n  (let [plat (platform)\n        record-file (str (fs/path (fs/parent dir) \"jolt-patches.edn\"))\n        prior (when (fs/exists? record-file) (edn/read-string (slurp record-file)))\n        ;; -z preserves the status column, spaces and rename paths. Renames\n        ;; cannot be a declared patch state and fail below as unknown paths.\n        ;; Gitignored undeclared files in the clone are invisible to git status.\n        status-result (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                               \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"status\" \"--porcelain=v1\" \"-z\")\n        _ (when-not (zero? (:exit status-result))\n            (patch-fail! \"git status failed: \" (:err status-result)))\n        status (:out status-result)\n        entries (remove str/blank? (str/split status #\"\\u0000\"))\n        _ (doseq [entry entries]\n            (when (or (< (count entry) 3)\n                      (not= \\space (nth entry 2))\n                      (some #{\\R \\C} (take 2 entry)))\n              (patch-fail! \"unsupported dirty/renamed path: \" (pr-str entry))))\n        dirty (set (map #(subs % 3) entries))\n        allowed (set (mapcat #(concat (keys (:files %))\n                                      (mapcat keys (vals (:generated %)))) patches))\n        unknown (set/difference dirty allowed)]\n    (when (seq unknown) (patch-fail! \"unknown dirty paths: \" (pr-str (sort unknown))))\n    (doseq [{:keys [id base path] expected :sha256} patches]\n      (when-not (= sha base) (patch-fail! id \" patch base \" base \" differs from pin \" sha))\n      (when-not (= expected (sha256 path)) (patch-fail! path \" sha256 mismatch\")))\n    (let [skip-requested? (= \"1\" (System/getenv \"JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_NO_APPLY\"))\n          test-dir (System/getenv \"JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR\")\n          _ (when (and skip-requested? (nil? test-dir))\n              (binding [*out* *err*]\n                (println \"WARNING: JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_NO_APPLY ignored without JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR\")))\n          no-apply? (and skip-requested? (some? test-dir))\n          live? (and (seq patches)\n                     (every? (fn [patch]\n                               (every? (fn [[path hashes]]\n                                         (= (:after hashes) (sha256 (fs/path dir path))))\n                                       (:files patch))) patches))\n          applied\n          (cond\n            no-apply? [] ; deliberately reach the behavioural gate on the old seed\n            live?\n            (do\n              (doseq [patch patches]\n                (check-digests! dir (get-in patch [:generated plat]) :after))\n              (println \"patches live\")\n              (mapv (fn [patch]\n                      (or (when (and (= sha (:base prior)) (= plat (:platform prior)))\n                            (some #(when (and (= (:id patch) (:id %))\n                                              (= (:sha256 patch) (:sha256 %))) %)\n                                  (:applied prior)))\n                          {:remint-passes 0})) patches))\n            :else\n            (do\n              (when (seq dirty) (patch-fail! \"partial patch state: \" (pr-str (sort dirty))))\n              (mapv\n                (fn [{:keys [id path files remint generated] :as patch}]\n                  (check-digests! dir files :before)\n                  (check-digests! dir (get generated plat) :before)\n                  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                                   \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"apply\" \"--check\" (str (fs/absolutize path)))]\n                    (when-not (zero? (:exit r)) (patch-fail! path \" patch rejected: \" (:err r))))\n                  (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"apply\" (str (fs/absolutize path)))\n                  (let [output (when remint\n                                 (let [tmp (str (fs/path dir \".git\" \"bootstrap-tmp\"))]\n                                   (fs/create-dirs tmp)\n                                   (sh {:dir dir :extra-env {\"JOLT_CHEZ\" scheme \"TMPDIR\" tmp}}\n                                       \"sh\" \"host/chez/remint.sh\")))\n                        passes (if remint\n                                 (some-> (re-find #\"converged after ([0-9]+) pass\" output) second parse-long)\n                                 0)]\n                    (when remint (println output))\n                    (when-not (and passes (<= 0 passes 8))\n                      (patch-fail! id \" remint did not report convergence within 8 passes\"))\n                    (check-digests! dir files :after)\n                    (check-digests! dir (get generated plat) :after)\n                    {:id id :sha256 (:sha256 patch) :remint-passes passes})) patches)))]\n      (smoke! dir scheme \"(+ 1 2)\" \"3\" \"jolt smoke failed\")\n      (doseq [{:keys [smoke]} patches]\n        (smoke! dir scheme (:form smoke) (:expect smoke) \"patch declared, not live\"))\n      (let [applied (mapv\n                      (fn [patch entry]\n                        (let [known (get-in patch [:generated plat])\n                              paths (keys (or known (some identity (vals (:generated patch)))))]\n                          (when (and (:remint patch) (nil? known))\n                            (println (:id patch) plat \"generated digests nil: :requalify; record and fill jolt-toolchain.edn\")\n                            (when (some #(and (= (:id patch) (:id %)) (:requalify %)) (:applied prior))\n                              (patch-fail! (:id patch) \" nil platform entry cannot be accepted twice; fill :generated \" plat)))\n                          (cond-> (assoc (dissoc entry :requalify) :id (:id patch) :sha256 (:sha256 patch)\n                                         :generated\n                                         (into {} (map (fn [path]\n                                                         (let [digest (sha256 (fs/path dir path))]\n                                                           (when-not digest (patch-fail! path \" generated file missing\"))\n                                                           [path {:before (get-in (or known (some identity (vals (:generated patch)))) [path :before])\n                                                                  :after digest}])) paths)))\n                            (and (:remint patch) (nil? known)) (assoc :requalify true))))\n                      patches applied)]\n        (spit record-file (str (pr-str {:base sha :applied applied :platform plat\n                                        :chez scheme :at (str (java.time.Instant/now))}) \"\\n\"))\n        record-file))))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
