{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '130,174p' src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj; sed -n '20,73p' bb.edn; sed -n '211,238p' native/jolt-crypto/jolt_crypto.c; sed -n '1160,1208p' native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp; sed -n '1235,1308p' /home/sto/ci/datomworld-j6ev/build/tools/jolt/host/chez/rt.ss\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(defn- patch-fail!\n  [& msg]\n  (apply fail! (concat msg [\"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- . && bb bootstrap:jolt\"])))\n\n\n(defn- sha256\n  [path]\n  (when (fs/regular-file? path)\n    (let [digest (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")]\n      (with-open [in (clojure.java.io/input-stream (str path))]\n        (let [buf (byte-array 65536)]\n          (loop []\n            (let [n (.read in buf)]\n              (when (pos? n) (.update digest buf 0 n) (recur))))))\n      (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and 255 %)) (.digest digest))))))\n\n\n(defn- platform\n  []\n  (case [(System/getProperty \"os.name\") (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    [\"Mac OS X\" \"aarch64\"] :darwin-arm64\n    [\"Linux\" \"amd64\"] :linux-x86_64\n    (patch-fail! \"unsupported patch platform\")))\n\n\n(defn- check-digests!\n  [dir files phase]\n  (doseq [[path hashes] files]\n    (when-not (= (phase hashes) (sha256 (fs/path dir path)))\n      (patch-fail! path \" sha256 mismatch (\" (name phase) \")\"))))\n\n\n(defn- smoke!\n  [dir scheme form expect message]\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true\n                    :extra-env {\"JOLT_CHEZ\" scheme \"JOLT_HOME\" dir}}\n                   (str (fs/path dir \"bin\" \"jolt\")) \"-e\" form)]\n    (when-not (and (zero? (:exit r)) (= expect (str/trim (:out r))))\n      (patch-fail! message \": \" (pr-str (:out r)) \" \" (:err r)))\n    (println \"jolt smoke\" form \"=>\" expect)))\n\n\n(defn- apply-patches!\n\n  test:jolt-bootstrap-neg\n  {:doc \"Copy/revert the jolt clone under gitignored build/bootstrap-neg (deleted on success, retained on failure) and declare a synthetic patch and prove bootstrap refuses it unapplied or corrupted, then accepts it applied (JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR selects the source clone)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\" \"--test-negative\")))}\n\n  smoke:jolt\n  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"-c\"\n                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\")))}\n\n  jolt\n  {:doc \"Run jolt -Srepro -M:jolt with the arguments given (a script path, -e ...), under build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"-c\"\n                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt \\\"$@\\\"\"\n                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  qualify:jolt-libcrypto\n  {:doc \"J1b requalification: print this platform's observed libcrypto identity {:canonical-path :version-num :version :sha256} for jolt-toolchain.edn :native :libcrypto :qualified (the digest from bb and from the library, required equal); changes nothing (needs a built wrapper: bb build:jolt-native, or --requalify after a library change)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj\")))}\n\n  probe:jolt-crypto\n  {:doc \"J1b: libcrypto provenance (qualified, missing, undeclared, version-floor, wrong-library-first, Linux LD_PRELOAD) and 256 MiB :blocking hash collect-safety, each in a child jolt process (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj\")))}\n\n  test:jolt-j5\n  {:doc \"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j5_acceptance.clj\")))}\n\n  probe:jolt-j5\n  {:doc \"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j5_run.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  calibrate:jolt-j5\n  {:doc \"J5b C4 + J5c: build the guards-off calibration variant of native/jolt-parser and record each nesting shape's stack cost per rule frame and per lookahead link on the 16 MiB parse thread (asserting every bound fits a quarter of the stack; writes build/j5b/calibration.edn), or, with --work, the work metric's per-shape counts and the corpus sweep the work bound derives from (writes build/j5b/work.edn; needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"-cp\" \"src/dev\"\n                         \"src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  probe:jolt-file\n  {:doc \"J4a: native/jolt-file gates, each in a child process: JVM-identical frame bytes (both hash algorithms), F2 s32BE prefixes, strict reads, injected short/EINTR/zero-progress/error transfers, corrupt-open byte identity, idempotent close, no fd or native-memory leak, a full collection during a 1 GiB :blocking pwrite, missing/wrong-layout wrapper refused before guest work, exported-symbol allowlist (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\")))}\n\n  probe:jolt-udp\n  {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\")))}\n      (void *)&EVP_sha256,                  (void *)&EVP_sha1,\n      (void *)&EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key,\n      (void *)&EVP_PKEY_new_raw_public_key, (void *)&EVP_PKEY_get_raw_public_key,\n      (void *)&EVP_DigestSignInit,          (void *)&EVP_DigestSign,\n      (void *)&EVP_DigestVerifyInit,        (void *)&EVP_DigestVerify,\n      (void *)&EVP_MD_CTX_new,              (void *)&EVP_MD_CTX_free,\n      (void *)&EVP_PKEY_free,               (void *)&OPENSSL_cleanse,\n      (void *)&OpenSSL_version_num,         (void *)&OpenSSL_version, (void *)&RAND_bytes};\n  const char *path = NULL;\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < sizeof entries / sizeof entries[0]; i++) {\n    Dl_info info;\n    if (!dladdr(entries[i], &info) || !info.dli_fname) return JC_DLADDR;\n    if (!path)\n      path = info.dli_fname;\n    else if (strcmp(path, info.dli_fname) != 0)\n      return JC_SPLIT;\n  }\n  char hex[65];\n  int status = file_sha256(path, hex);\n  if (status != JC_OK) return status;\n  int n = snprintf(buf, cap, \"%lu\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\", (unsigned long)OpenSSL_version_num(),\n                   OpenSSL_version(OPENSSL_VERSION), path, hex);\n  if (n < 0 || (size_t)n >= cap) return JC_SPACE;\n  return n;\n}\n\n// A new worker owning fresh DFA vectors and PredictionContextCaches. NULL when\n// it cannot be made (nothing throws across the boundary).\nJOLT_EXPORT void* jolt_parser_worker_new(void) {\n  try {\n    return new Worker(published_atns());\n  } catch (...) {\n    return nullptr;\n  }\n}\n\n// Dispose a worker and its caches. NULL is accepted. The caller must not use\n// the handle again, nor free it while a call on it runs. The caches are\n// destroyed on a parse thread: a cached prediction-context chain is destroyed\n// recursively, as deep as the lookahead bound allows. When no parse thread\n// can be started the worker is leaked, never destroyed on the caller's stack.\nJOLT_EXPORT void jolt_parser_worker_free(void* w) {\n  if (Worker* worker = as_worker(w)) {\n    worker->tag = 0;\n    Job job{free_job, worker, {}, -3};\n    uint8_t* msg = nullptr;\n    size_t msg_len = 0;\n    on_parse_thread(job, &msg, &msg_len);\n    std::free(msg);\n  }\n}\n\n// Parse UTF-8 `src[0, len)` from `file_input` with `worker`'s caches and\n// answer the exporter's records (layout \"JPX1\" above). Statuses as\n// jolt_parser_parse, plus -5; -1 also for a NULL or unrecognized worker.\nJOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_export(void* worker, const uint8_t* src,\n                                       size_t len, uint8_t** out,\n                                       size_t* out_len) {\n  if (!out || !out_len || (!src && len != 0)) return -1;\n  *out = nullptr;\n  *out_len = 0;\n  Worker* w = as_worker(worker);\n  if (!w) return -1;\n  if (int32_t refused = over_input(len, out, out_len)) return refused;\n  Hold hold(w);\n  if (!hold.held) return -5;\n  Call call{w, src, len, out, out_len};\n  Job job{export_job, &call, {}, -3, true};\n  return on_parse_thread(job, out, out_len);\n}\n\n// Parse UTF-8 `src[0, len)` from the `file_input` rule, with the generated\n// static caches (the round-1 probe surface).\nJOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_parse(const uint8_t* src, size_t len,\n;; Installed once, at the end of this file, at load, on every driver, so a gate\n;; booting the runtime from source has it as much as a built binary does. The\n;; threshold goes in as a thunk the watch reads at each wait, so the switch can\n;; be read again at process start (jolt-install-gc-policy!: a built heap ran\n;; this file in the BUILD's process, and the switch is the running one's) and\n;; the threshold changed by on-gc-stall, without installing again. At the END\n;; so that everything the report calls (locks.ss, printing.ss, lazy-bridge.ss)\n;; is loaded before the first rendezvous that could take the timeout.\n(define jolt-ffi-callbacks-active (box 0))\n(define jolt-gc-stall-default-seconds 2)\n(define jolt-gc-stall-env-seconds #f)       ; JOLT_GC_STALL's threshold, #f = off\n(define jolt-gc-stall-reporter #f)          ; on-gc-stall's procedure, or #f\n(define jolt-gc-stall-reporter-seconds #f)  ; its own threshold, or #f\n(define jolt-gc-stall-watch-installed? #f)\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-seconds)\n  (or jolt-gc-stall-reporter-seconds jolt-gc-stall-env-seconds\n      jolt-gc-stall-default-seconds))\n;; #f when the report is off, else the threshold in seconds.\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-from-env)\n  (let ((v (getenv \"JOLT_GC_STALL\")))\n    (cond ((not (jolt-env-flag? \"JOLT_GC_STALL\")) #f)\n          ((member (string-downcase v) '(\"1\" \"true\" \"on\")) jolt-gc-stall-default-seconds)\n          (else (let ((n (string->number v)))\n                  (if (jolt-gc-stall-threshold? n)\n                      n\n                      (gc-config-error \"JOLT_GC_STALL\" v\n                                       \"1, true, on, or a threshold in seconds\")))))))\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-threshold? n)\n  (and n (real? n) (> n 0) (< n 86400)))\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-setup!)\n  (set! jolt-gc-stall-env-seconds (jolt-gc-stall-from-env)))\n;; PROC (seconds threads callbacks message) or #f for the default report;\n;; SECONDS a threshold or #f for JOLT_GC_STALL's (or the default). Answers\n;; whether this target has the watch at all.\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-set-reporter! proc seconds)\n  (set! jolt-gc-stall-reporter-seconds (and proc seconds))\n  (set! jolt-gc-stall-reporter proc)\n  jolt-gc-stall-watch-installed?)\n(define (jolt-on-foreign-thread?)\n  (let ((id (get-thread-id)))\n    (and (not (eqv? id jolt-boot-thread-id))\n         (not (jolt-started-thread? id)))))\n(define (jolt-gc-stall-message seconds unreached callbacks)\n  (format\n    (string-append\n      \"jolt.ffi: a garbage collection has been waiting ~a s for ~a thread~a to reach a safe point.\\n\"\n      \"  Every thread running jolt code reaches one within microseconds. A thread parked in a\\n\"\n      \"  foreign call that is not marked :blocking never does, and every other thread now waits\\n\"\n      \"  for that call to return.\"\n      (if (> callbacks 0)\n          (string-append\n            \" ~a :collect-safe callback~a in progress: if the parked call is\\n\"\n            \"  waiting for its answer, the two wait for each other for good.\")\n          \"~a~a\")\n      \" Mark the outbound call\\n\"\n      \"  :blocking — see the :collect-safe notes on foreign-callable in jolt.ffi.\\n\")\n    seconds unreached (if (= unreached 1) \"\" \"s\")\n    (if (> callbacks 0) callbacks \"\")\n    (cond ((= callbacks 0) \"\") ((= callbacks 1) \" is\") (else \"s are\"))))\n(define (jolt-report-gc-stall unreached)\n  (let ((reporter jolt-gc-stall-reporter))\n    (when (or reporter jolt-gc-stall-env-seconds)\n      (let* ((callbacks (max (unbox jolt-ffi-callbacks-active)\n                             (if (jolt-on-foreign-thread?) 1 0)))\n             (seconds (jolt-gc-stall-seconds))\n             (message (jolt-gc-stall-message seconds unreached callbacks)))\n        (if reporter\n            (guard (_ (#t #f)) (reporter seconds unreached callbacks message))\n            (jolt-eprint message))))))\n\n(load \"host/chez/collections.ss\")\n(load \"host/chez/seq.ss\")\n\n;; --- version ------------------------------------------------------------------\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The plan will gate each FFI capability separately, retaining refusal tests for every unsupported operation. P2 and P3 will require explicit Gambit launchers: the current qualification scripts hardcode the Chez launcher. I’ll also call out two delivery prerequisites: `qualify:jolt-upgrade` is documented but absent from `bb.edn`, and the patch verifier needs final-tree validation before successive patches can safely touch the same files.\n"}}
